# Tool Input Validation

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Issue | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | Draft |

The registry validates the same JSON Schema supplied to providers before domain executors receive model input.

## Contract

1. "'`execute` returns a corrective `ToolResponse` for missing required properties, wrong types and invalid enum members without invoking the executor; rejection text and logs name the property and constraint without exposing input values, while valid input including unknown properties passes through unchanged exactly once, with no coercion or defaults and the existing unknown-tool exception preserved.
2. Static schemas compile at registration, reject uncompilable schemas with the tool name, and reuse the compiled validator across executions.
3. Function-valued definitions resolve on every execution and validate against the current schema, caching compilation by resolved schema object identity.

## Integration and release obligations

Rejection results feed back into the existing orchestrator tool loop so the model can correct its call within the default five-round limit; unknown names continue to throw `Unknown tool: <name>`.

The implementation adds a runtime JSON Schema validator dependency, documents this contract in README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md, and links here from a one-line execute comment.

The release includes a MINOR version bump and an npm-facing changelog entry explaining that executors no longer receive malformed input, including tools that previously produced their own validation errors.
